# Local rules first

- Before acting, read `.cursor/rules/` in this repo.
- Project rules override Cursor defaults and global user rules when they conflict.
- Do not follow a general habit (for example browser verification) if a local rule says otherwise.
- Example: `.cursor/rules/browser-verification.mdc` forbids opening the browser unless the user asks. That wins over any global “verify UI in the browser” instruction.
